A||||4||Kerri 98||Sail Panels from Paul McKibben||||6||
Z||000000||Kerri 98||05-27-2001||04:16 PM||||Someone special to me recently ordered some sail panels as a birthday present. The panels arrived before my birthday directly from Paul McKibbons (Even had a sticky note with a Happy Birthday note inside requested to be placed by the sender, hehe). I just have completed putting them on my car using Phil Stevens method of installing with the frames on the car.  My frames were relatively in good shape and didn't require painting. My old sail panels, however were extremely faded and were cracked in several places. Using Phil's method I completed the job in 35 minutes, both sides.  The 3M General Purpose Adhesive Cleaner worked beautifully. (If only I could have found that stuff at the first place I went to) I found it finally at Ace Hardware and was close to $11.00. The only advice I would add would be to wear safety glasses while you are removing the old panels.  Mine were extremely brittle and were like sharp glass slivers as I removed them. Sure wouldn't be much fun if you couldn't enjoy looking at those awesome new sail panels because of a patch on your eye.<BR>Thanks Paul and Phil..and Sender of my panels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">..Kerri||||reg||6
